Third-Party Software Used by PDF Export
=======================================

handoff-mcp (MIT) can export documents to PDF.

* The Typst compiler is BUNDLED: release builds (--features bundled-typst)
  statically link it, through the typst-as-lib wrapper and the typst, typst-pdf
  and related typst-* crates. See "Bundled" below. Plain `cargo build` without
  the feature does not link it and falls back to a Typst CLI the USER installs.
* Mermaid CLI and a headless Chrome are NOT bundled. They are optional, user-
  installed, discovered on PATH (or via HANDOFF_MMDC_BIN / HANDOFF_CHROME_BIN)
  and run as separate processes; their licenses bind the user's own
  installation, not handoff-mcp's distribution. They are listed here so the
  compatibility check is on record.

The full list of Rust crates statically linked into the handoff-mcp binaries,
including every transitive dependency of the bundled Typst compiler, is in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (generated by scripts/generate-third-party-licenses.sh
with --features bundled-typst; verified by `cargo deny check`).

Bundled
-------

typst-as-lib                 Typst compiler wrapper (library)
  Home:      https://github.com/Relacibo/typst-as-lib
  License:   MIT

typst, typst-pdf, typst-library, typst-layout, typst-eval, typst-syntax, ...
  Home:      https://github.com/typst/typst
  License:   Apache-2.0 (the NOTICE of the upstream project lists its own
             third-party components; each linked crate's license text is
             reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md)
  Version:   all typst-* compiler crates are released in lockstep and must
             resolve to one version (scripts/check-typst-versions.sh, run in
             lefthook pre-push and CI)
  Used for:  compiling the Markdown-derived .typ source to PDF in-process

typst-assets                 Latin fonts embedded by the typst-kit-embed-fonts
  Home:      https://github.com/typst/typst-assets
  License:   Apache-2.0 for the crate; the embedded font files keep their own
             licenses (Libertinus Serif, New Computer Modern, DejaVu Sans Mono:
             SIL Open Font License 1.1 / GUST Font License / Bitstream Vera).
             No CJK font is embedded.

option-ext                   (transitive, via typst-as-lib)
  License:   MPL-2.0, used unmodified from crates.io (file-level copyleft:
             allowed by deny.toml only for this crate).

Tools (not bundled)
-------------------

Typst CLI                    Only without --features bundled-typst
  Home:      https://github.com/typst/typst
  License:   Apache-2.0 (LICENSE and NOTICE shipped in every release archive;
             the NOTICE lists Typst's own MIT/other third-party components)
  Minimum:   0.12.0
  Install:   brew install typst | winget install --id Typst.Typst |
             snap install typst | cargo install --locked typst-cli |
             release archives at https://github.com/typst/typst/releases
  Used for:  `typst compile` (Markdown-derived .typ -> PDF) and `typst fonts`
             (Japanese font detection)

Mermaid CLI (mmdc)           OPTIONAL (Mermaid diagrams)
  Home:      https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid-cli
  License:   MIT (package @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli; its dependency mermaid is
             MIT, puppeteer is Apache-2.0)
  Minimum:   10.0.0
  Install:   npm install -g @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli
  Used for:  rendering ```mermaid blocks to SVG. Without it, Mermaid blocks
             stay as code blocks and the export response carries a warning.

chrome-headless-shell        OPTIONAL (needed by mmdc)
  Home:      https://pptr.dev/browsers-api/ (Chrome for Testing /
             Chromium)
  License:   Chromium project licenses: BSD-3-Clause for Chromium's own code,
             plus bundled third-party components under their own licenses
             (see the LICENSE file shipped with the browser build you
             install). Puppeteer, which downloads it, is Apache-2.0.
  Minimum:   none enforced by handoff-mcp (mmdc's Puppeteer must be able to
             drive it). chrome-headless-shell, Google Chrome and Chromium are
             all accepted.
  Install:   npx puppeteer browsers install chrome-headless-shell |
             OS package for Chrome / Chromium
  Used for:  headless rendering inside mmdc

Japanese fonts (not bundled)
----------------------------

Japanese text needs a Japanese font installed on the system. handoff-mcp
ships no CJK font. Detected families, in preference order: Noto Sans/Serif CJK JP
(SIL Open Font License 1.1), IPAex/IPA Gothic and Mincho (IPA Font License
v1.0), and the macOS / Windows system Japanese fonts.

Compatibility summary
---------------------

| Tool                  | License                   | Compatible with MIT handoff-mcp |
|-----------------------|---------------------------|---------------------------------|
| typst-* crates        | Apache-2.0                | Yes (statically linked)         |
| typst-as-lib          | MIT                       | Yes (statically linked)         |
| Typst CLI             | Apache-2.0                | Yes (separate process, fallback)|
| Mermaid CLI (mmdc)    | MIT                       | Yes (separate process)          |
| chrome-headless-shell | Chromium (BSD-3-Clause +) | Yes (separate process)          |

No GPL-family tool is required (REQ-PDF-009 AC2). Re-check this file whenever
a tool is added to src/storage/docs/pdf/deps.rs or a minimum version changes.
